  1	---
  2	name: verify
  3	description: Drive the Exposed Svelte search UI against its Rust API and PostgreSQL database. Use after changes to search, result display, keyboard controls, URL state, or frontend/API integration to capture browser and database evidence.
  4	---
  5	
  6	# Verify Exposed search
  7	
  8	Read the [feature map](features/README.md), then the affected feature files. The primary user path is the search page. The Rust `/search` endpoint supports it. Data ingestion commands and the legacy Python importer are separate workflows described in the repository README.
  9	
 10	Run commands from the repository root in a dedicated Git worktree. Use Bash for the shell blocks. Requirements are Docker Compose, SQLx CLI 0.9.0, Python 3, Node.js 24+, npm, and curl. There is no application login.
 11	
 12	## Launch
 13	
 14	Use an unused verification worktree with no `.env` or `.env.compose`. The setup script writes both files. Do not replace an existing development environment. Each worktree gets separate ports, containers, and volumes. Drive one session per worktree.
 15	
 16	```bash
 17	set -euo pipefail
 18	cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
 19	test -f .git
 20	test ! -e .env
 21	test ! -e .env.compose
 22	mkdir -p target/verification
 23	export VERIFY_EVIDENCE="$(mktemp -d "$PWD/target/verification/run.XXXXXX")"
 24	git rev-parse HEAD > "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/revision.txt"
 25	git diff HEAD > "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/source.diff"
 26	python3 .agents/skills/setup-env/scripts/setup-compose.py \
 27		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/setup.log"
 28	set -a
 29	source .env.compose
 30	source .env
 31	set +a
 32	export VERIFY_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:$FRONTEND_PORT"
 33	export VERIFY_API_URL="http://127.0.0.1:$API_PORT"
 34	cp .env.compose "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/compose.env"
 35	printf '%s\n' "$PWD" > "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/worktree.txt"
 36	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
 37		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" up -d --wait postgres
 38	sqlx migrate run > "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/migrations.log" 2>&1
 39	```
 40	
 41	Seed the empty database with the repository's existing test fixtures. These are synthetic test records, not a current Parliament import. `John` returns two MPs, `McDonald's` returns a company, and `Aaron Banks` returns an individual funder. `HSBC` has no match in this fixture set.
 42	
 43	```bash
 44	test "$(docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
 45		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" exec -T postgres \
 46		psql -X -U exposed -d exposed -Atc 'SELECT count(*) FROM exposed.members')" = 0
 47	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
 48		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" exec -T postgres \
 49		psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -U exposed -d exposed \
 50		< db/fixtures/add_members.sql > "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/seed.log"
 51	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
 52		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" exec -T postgres \
 53		psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -U exposed -d exposed \
 54		< db/fixtures/add_declarations_and_funding_entries.sql >> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/seed.log"
 55	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
 56		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" up -d --build exposed frontend \
 57		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/launch.log" 2>&1
 58	npm --prefix frontend ci --no-audit --no-fund
 59	(cd frontend && PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=0 npx playwright install chromium)
 60	curl --fail --silent --show-error --retry 90 --retry-delay 2 \
 61		--retry-all-errors --max-time 3 \
 62		"$VERIFY_BASE_URL/api/search?term=John&max_entries=10&strictness=1" \
 63		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/ready.json"
 64	```
 65	
 66	Readiness requires an HTTP 200 from that proxied search with both fixture MPs. The Rust log says `Listening on http://localhost:6999` inside the container. A frontend HTML response alone does not establish API readiness. The first Rust build can take longer than the frontend startup. If the bounded retry fails, inspect the Compose logs, run Doctor, and clean up before retrying.
 67	
 68	The current checkout contains a later migration that removes term tables as well as the initial baseline. Apply the checked-in migrations as they are. Do not change migration history to run this skill. See `db/README.md` for schema work.
 69	
 70	## Doctor
 71	
 72	Run this read-only check before driving and whenever an instance looks wrong. It checks container ownership, the source mount, running state, the Vite proxy, and the expected database fixtures. A failed check means the instance is not ready to drive.
 73	
 74	```bash
 75	(
 76		set -euo pipefail
 77		for service in postgres exposed frontend; do
 78			container="$(docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
 79				-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" ps -q "$service")"
 80			test -n "$container"
 81			test "$(docker inspect -f '{{.State.Running}}' "$container")" = true
 82			test "$(docker inspect -f '{{index .Config.Labels "com.docker.compose.project.working_dir"}}' "$container")" = "$PWD"
 83			if test "$service" = exposed; then
 84				test "$(docker inspect -f '{{range .Mounts}}{{if eq .Destination "/app"}}{{.Source}}{{end}}{{end}}' "$container")" = "$PWD"
 85			fi
 86		done
 87		curl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 5 \
 88			"$VERIFY_BASE_URL/api/search?term=John&max_entries=10&strictness=1" |
 89			python3 -c 'import json,sys; rows=json.load(sys.stdin)["entities"]; assert len(rows)==2 and {r["name"] for r in rows}=={"John McDonnell","John Humphries"} and all(r["kind"]=="MP" for r in rows); print("Doctor passed: owned stack, real API, expected MPs")'
 90	) | tee "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/doctor.log"
 91	```
 92	
 93	Source edits are bind-mounted. Before proving a Rust change, require its rebuild to finish in the `exposed` log and then rerun Doctor. Doctor is a readiness check, not proof of the changed behavior.
 94	
 95	## Drive
 96	
 97	Capture the database before browser actions. PostgreSQL 18's fixed dump restriction key makes the two local snapshots comparable.
 98	
 99	```bash
100	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
101		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" exec -T postgres \
102		pg_dump -U exposed -d exposed --data-only --schema=exposed \
103		--no-owner --restrict-key=ExposedVerification \
104		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/database-before.sql"
105	PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=0 \
106		frontend/.agents/skills/verify/scripts/search.mjs \
107		"$VERIFY_BASE_URL" "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/search" \
108		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/search.log" 2>&1
109	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file .env.compose \
110		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" exec -T postgres \
111		pg_dump -U exposed -d exposed --data-only --schema=exposed \
112		--no-owner --restrict-key=ExposedVerification \
113		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/database-after.sql"
114	cmp "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/database-before.sql" "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/database-after.sql"
115	```
116	
117	The helper uses the installed Playwright package and its Chromium browser. It launches a fresh browser context, exercises the short-query gate, focuses search with `/`, types `John`, compares visible names with the real response, and clears with the button. It closes its browser even after an assertion fails. Exit code 0 and `search/proof.json` establish this path. Other mapped entry points still need their own actions.
118	
119	For another feature, copy the helper to a unique `.mjs` file beside it so Node can resolve `frontend/node_modules`. Adapt its actions using the matching feature recipe, and pass a new evidence subdirectory. Keep its trace, failure capture, and browser cleanup. Remove that temporary script in Cleanup. Do not register `page.route` handlers for live proof.
120	
121	The existing `frontend/tests/search.spec.ts` suite controls the API with fabricated responses. Use it to supplement cancellation and error-edge checks, and label its output as frontend-only. It is not evidence that Rust or PostgreSQL worked. Its fixed port 4173 and server reuse also need care. Run it with `CI=1` and only when port 4173 is free.
122	
123	## Evidence
124	
125	Keep all proof under the printed absolute `$VERIFY_EVIDENCE` path, inside the worktree's ignored `target/verification/`. Do not use `frontend/test-results` for durable proof because another Playwright test run can clear it.
126	
127	The helper preserves `trace.zip`, before/result/cleared screenshots, ARIA snapshots, the real `response.json`, and a `proof.json` with the feature ID and entry points. Failures retain `failure.txt` and a screenshot when a page exists. The trace records actions and network responses, not only the final page.
128	
129	Pair each claimed entry point with its action and observable result. Compare real API ordering and spelling with the UI. Compare database snapshots for search's absence of writes. For future mutating features, inspect the stored row or file after the user action. Mock only an external system behind an existing production boundary, and identify that limitation in the proof. Do not substitute internal state setters or test-only endpoints for the user path.
130	
131	This workflow has no dry-run mode. It writes fixtures to a disposable database, starts local containers, and may download images, dependencies, and Chromium. It does not fetch Parliament data. If a future command claims to be a dry-run, check its files, requests, and Git refs before and after instead of trusting the flag.
132	
133	## Cleanup
134	
135	Run cleanup after every attempt, including failed launches or browser assertions. The saved Compose environment identifies this run even after a shell restart. Set `VERIFY_EVIDENCE` to the recorded run directory when resuming. Do not remove the evidence directory.
136	
137	```bash
138	test "$(cat "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/worktree.txt")" = "$PWD"
139	set -a
140	source "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/compose.env"
141	set +a
142	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/compose.env" \
143		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" logs --no-color \
144		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/compose.log" 2>&1
145	docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/compose.env" \
146		-p "$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME" down --volumes \
147		> "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/cleanup.log" 2>&1
148	test -z "$(docker ps -aq --filter "label=com.docker.compose.project=$COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME")"
149	rm -f .env .env.compose
150	test -s "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/cleanup.log"
151	printf 'Evidence retained at %s\n' "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE"
152	```
153	
154	`down --volumes` removes only this disposable Compose project's instances, database, and dependency volumes. Host dependencies and Docker image caches can remain. Remove any temporary driver copy you created by its exact path. Never kill by process name or stop another project's containers. After a successful proof, confirm `search/proof.json` and `search/trace.zip` still exist after cleanup. After a failed attempt, preserve its logs and any failure artifacts.
155	
156	## Helpers
157	
158	- Execute `scripts/search.mjs` as shown in Drive. Its arguments are the owned frontend's loopback URL and a new evidence subdirectory. It requires the fixture database.
159	- Reuse `.agents/skills/setup-env/scripts/setup-compose.py` from the repository root for environment setup. It selects free ports and writes the matching `DATABASE_URL`. Do not rerun it against a running stack.
160	- Open a saved trace with `cd frontend && npx playwright show-trace "$VERIFY_EVIDENCE/search/trace.zip"`.
161	
162	Use `/maintain-verification-skill` when app changes require updates to these recipes or the feature map.
  1	#!/usr/bin/env node
  2	import assert from "node:assert/strict";
  3	import { mkdir, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
  4	import { resolve } from "node:path";
  5	import { chromium, expect } from "@playwright/test";
  6	
  7	const [baseURL, evidenceDirectory] = process.argv.slice(2);
  8	assert(baseURL && evidenceDirectory, "Usage: search.mjs <loopback-url> <new-evidence-directory>");
  9	const origin = new URL(baseURL);
 10	assert(
 11	  origin.protocol === "http:" &&
 12	    ["127.0.0.1", "localhost"].includes(origin.hostname) &&
 13	    !origin.username && !origin.password && origin.href === `${origin.origin}/`,
 14	  "Use the owned frontend's HTTP loopback origin without a path or credentials",
 15	);
 16	const evidence = resolve(evidenceDirectory);
 17	await mkdir(evidence);
 18	const browser = await chromium.launch();
 19	try {
 20	  const context = await browser.newContext({ baseURL: origin.origin });
 21	  await context.tracing.start({ screenshots: true, snapshots: true, sources: true });
 22	  const page = await context.newPage();
 23	  page.setDefaultTimeout(15_000);
 24	  const requests = [];
 25	  const pageErrors = [];
 26	  page.on("request", (request) => {
 27	    if (new URL(request.url()).pathname === "/api/search") requests.push(request.url());
 28	  });
 29	  page.on("pageerror", (error) => pageErrors.push(error.message));
 30	  try {
 31	    console.log("Open Exposed and focus search with the slash shortcut.");
 32	    await page.goto("/");
 33	    await expect(page.getByRole("link", { name: "Exposed home" })).toBeVisible();
 34	    await expect(page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Start with a name" })).toBeVisible();
 35	    await page.screenshot({ path: `${evidence}/before.png`, fullPage: true });
 36	    await writeFile(`${evidence}/before.aria.txt`, await page.locator("body").ariaSnapshot());
 37	    await page.keyboard.press("/");
 38	    const input = page.getByRole("searchbox", { name: "Search MPs and funders" });
 39	    await expect(input).toBeFocused();
 40	
 41	    console.log("Enter a two-character query and submit; search must stay idle.");
 42	    await input.fill("Jo");
 43	    await input.press("Enter");
 44	    await expect(page.getByText("Type 1 more character to search.")).toBeVisible();
 45	    await expect(page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Start with a name" })).toBeVisible();
 46	    assert.deepEqual(requests, []);
 47	
 48	    console.log("Type John and compare rendered names with the real API response.");
 49	    const responsePromise = page.waitForResponse((response) => {
 50	      const url = new URL(response.url());
 51	      return url.pathname === "/api/search" && url.searchParams.get("term") === "John";
 52	    });
 53	    await input.fill("  John  ");
 54	    const response = await responsePromise;
 55	    const bodyText = await response.text();
 56	    await writeFile(`${evidence}/response.json`, bodyText);
 57	    assert.equal(response.status(), 200);
 58	    const body = JSON.parse(bodyText);
 59	    assert.deepEqual(
 60	      [...body.entities].sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name)),
 61	      [
 62	        { name: "John Humphries", kind: "MP", funder_kind: null },
 63	        { name: "John McDonnell", kind: "MP", funder_kind: null },
 64	      ],
 65	    );
 66	    const request = new URL(response.url());
 67	    assert.equal(request.searchParams.get("max_entries"), "10");
 68	    assert.equal(request.searchParams.get("strictness"), "1");
 69	    await expect(page.getByRole("heading", { name: "2 results shown" })).toBeVisible();
 70	    await expect(page.locator(".entity-name")).toHaveText(body.entities.map((entity) => entity.name));
 71	    await expect(page.getByRole("button", { name: "MP", exact: true })).toHaveCount(2);
 72	    await expect(page.locator(".entity-name mark")).toHaveText(["John", "John"]);
 73	    assert.equal(new URL(page.url()).searchParams.get("q"), "John");
 74	    await page.screenshot({ path: `${evidence}/results.png`, fullPage: true });
 75	    await writeFile(`${evidence}/results.aria.txt`, await page.locator("body").ariaSnapshot());
 76	
 77	    console.log("Click Clear search and verify the idle state, focus, and URL.");
 78	    await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Clear search" }).click();
 79	    await expect(input).toHaveValue("");
 80	    await expect(input).toBeFocused();
 81	    await expect(page.getByRole("heading", { name: "Start with a name" })).toBeVisible();
 82	    await expect(page.locator(".entity-row")).toHaveCount(0);
 83	    assert.equal(new URL(page.url()).searchParams.has("q"), false);
 84	    assert.deepEqual(pageErrors, []);
 85	    await page.screenshot({ path: `${evidence}/cleared.png`, fullPage: true });
 86	    await writeFile(`${evidence}/cleared.aria.txt`, await page.locator("body").ariaSnapshot());
 87	    await writeFile(`${evidence}/proof.json`, JSON.stringify({
 88	      feature: "search-controls",
 89	      entryPoints: ["slash shortcut", "short-query Enter", "typed search", "Clear search button"],
 90	      baseURL: origin.origin,
 91	      requests,
 92	      entities: body.entities,
 93	      pageErrors,
 94	      result: "passed",
 95	    }, null, 2));
 96	    console.log(`Search controls passed. Evidence: ${evidence}`);
 97	  } catch (error) {
 98	    await writeFile(`${evidence}/failure.txt`, String(error.stack ?? error));
 99	    await page.screenshot({ path: `${evidence}/failure.png`, fullPage: true });
100	    throw error;
101	  } finally {
102	    await context.tracing.stop({ path: `${evidence}/trace.zip` });
103	  }
104	} finally {
105	  await browser.close();
106	}
